  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Proverbs",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 17,
    "summary": "He who is glad at calamities will be punished—A friend loves at all times—Even a fool, when he holds his peace, is counted wise.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Better is a dry morsel, and quietness therewith, than an house full of sacrifices with strife.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "Prov. 15:17."
          },
          {
            "start": 87,
            "end": 93,
            "text": "TG Strife."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 9
          },
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 86
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A wise servant shall have rule over a son that causeth shame, and shall have part of the inheritance among the brethren.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "TG Servant."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The fining pot is for silver, and the furnace for gold: but the Lord trieth the hearts.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "Mal. 3:3 (2–3); D&C 128:24."
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 75,
            "text": "TG Test."
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 86,
            "text": "Jer. 17:10."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 17
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A wicked doer giveth heed to false lips; and a liar giveth ear to a naughty tongue.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whoso mocketh the poor reproacheth his Maker: and he that is glad at calamities shall not be unpunished.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "Prov. 14:31; Mosiah 4:17 (16–18). TG Mocking."
          },
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "TG Poor."
          },
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 65,
            "text": "Job 31:29 (28–29); Prov. 24:17; Obad. 1:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 49
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Children’s children are the crown of old men; and the glory of children are their fathers.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "TG Family, Love within; Family, Patriarchal."
          },
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "TG Family, Children, Duties of; Marriage, Fatherhood."
          },
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 59,
            "text": "TG Glory."
          },
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "TG Children."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 23
          },
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 75
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Excellent speech becometh not a fool: much less do lying lips a prince.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "TG Communication."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A gift is as a precious stone in the eyes of him that hath it: whithersoever it turneth, it prospereth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 12
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that covereth a transgression seeketh love; but he that repeateth a matter separateth very friends.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 32,
            "text": "IE forgives a transgression."
          },
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "IE promotes a loving relationship."
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "D&C 64:9 (9–10)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 89,
            "end": 93
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A reproof entereth more into a wise man than an hundred stripes into a fool.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 9,
            "text": "TG Reproof."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "An evil man seeketh only rebellion: therefore a cruel messenger shall be sent against him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "TG Rebellion."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 11
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Let a bear robbed of her whelps meet a man, rather than a fool in his folly.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "Hosea 13:8."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whoso rewardeth evil for good, evil shall not depart from his house.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "TG Reward."
          },
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "TG Evil."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The beginning of strife is as when one letteth out water: therefore leave off contention, before it be meddled with.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "Prov. 25:8."
          },
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 88,
            "text": "D&C 136:23 (23–34)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 29
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that justifieth the wicked, and he that condemneth the just, even they both are abomination to the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "TG Injustice."
          },
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "Prov. 24:24; Isa. 5:23."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 82
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore is there a price in the hand of a fool to get wisdom, seeing he hath no heart to it?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 18
          },
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 78
          },
          {
            "start": 88,
            "end": 94
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A friend loveth at all times, and a brother is born for adversity.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "TG Friendship."
          },
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "TG Brotherhood and Sisterhood."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A man void of understanding striketh hands, and becometh surety in the presence of his friend.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 47
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He loveth transgression that loveth strife: and he that exalteth his gate seeketh destruction.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 64,
            "text": "Prov. 29:23."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 47
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that hath a froward heart findeth no good: and he that hath a perverse tongue falleth into mischief.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "Ps. 101:4."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that begetteth a fool doeth it to his sorrow: and the father of a fool hath no joy.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "Prov. 10:1; 17:25."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 33
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A merry heart doeth good like a medicine: but a broken spirit drieth the bones.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "TG Cheerful."
          },
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "Prov. 15:13; D&C 59:15 (14–16)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 29
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A wicked man taketh a gift out of the bosom to pervert the ways of judgment.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "TG Bribe."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 12
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Wisdom is before him that hath understanding; but the eyes of a fool are in the ends of the earth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 44,
            "text": "Prov. 14:6."
          },
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "Eccl. 2:14."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 9
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 72
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A foolish son is a grief to his father, and bitterness to her that bare him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 9,
            "text": "Prov. 17:21."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 16
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Also to punish the just is not good, nor to strike princes for equity.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 26
          },
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 40
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that hath knowledge spareth his words: and a man of understanding is of an excellent spirit.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 30,
            "text": "Prov. 10:19; James 1:19."
          },
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 68,
            "text": "TG Understanding."
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "HEB is cool of spirit (i.e., reserved)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 45
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Even a fool, when he holdeth his peace, is counted wise: and he that shutteth his lips is esteemed a man of understanding.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "Job 13:5."
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "Prov. 29:11; Amos 5:13."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 60
          },
          {
            "start": 87,
            "end": 98
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
